{
  "Tiles of different sizes packed on a grid of base cells: a tile is so many cells wide and tall. They fill the height in columns and scroll sideways, or fill the width in rows; they can be chosen, and put in another order by dragging.": "",
  "Tiles on a grid": "",
  "`baseItemWidth` and `baseItemHeight` are one cell; a tile’s `widthRatio` and `heightRatio` say how many it takes. Down the columns (`horizontal`, the default) the view needs a `height` and scrolls sideways; the tiles are packed so no cell stays empty where a later tile fits.": "",
  "Choosing tiles": "",
  "`selectionMode` makes the tiles options: `single` keeps one, `multiple` any number (Ctrl and a press, or Space, adds and takes away). `value` is the chosen tile’s `key`, else its index, or a list of them; `x-model` binds it two-way. The arrow keys walk the grid by where the tiles lie.": "",
  "Another order": "",
  "With `allowReorder` a tile is dragged to its new place (a long press on a touch screen) or moved with Ctrl and an arrow key. The tile moves and `onReordered` tells the indexes: reorder your data there, as the example does, so the next draw agrees.": "",
  "An item’s `content` makes the tile’s content when the tile is made; what is in it works as anywhere else, and a press on a button inside is that button’s. `onItemClick` tells a press on the tile itself.": "",
  "One stop: the tile focused last, else the first chosen, else the first.": "",
  "The nearest tile that way, by where the tiles lie; Home and End the first and the last.": "",
  "Chooses the tile (`single`), or chooses it or lets it go (`multiple`).": "",
  "A press on the tile: `onItemClick`, and the choice as a press makes it.": "",
  "With `allowReorder`: moves the tile a place back or on; Ctrl + Home and End to the ends. The move is read out.": "",
  "A `list` of `listitem`s without selection; a `listbox` of `option`s with it (`aria-multiselectable` for `multiple`), each `aria-selected`.": "",
  "`aria-disabled`, skipped by the keys, not chosen by a press.": "",
  "A copy of the tile follows the pointer; the tile where the drop would land is marked; Escape lets go. On a touch screen a long press lifts the tile.": "",
  "The view. `data-direction`, `data-reorder`, `data-dragging` while a tile is dragged.": "",
  "A tile. `aria-selected`, `aria-disabled`, `data-dragging` (left faint in its place), `data-drop=\"before|after\"` where the drop would land.": "",
  "A tile’s text; the copy after the pointer.": "",
  "Units: a tile (`hover`, `pressed`, `focus`, `selected`, `disabled`, `dragging`, `target`), its text, the copy after the pointer, the view.": "",
  "Between the tiles.": "",
  "The tiles in order: `TileViewItem`s (`text`, `widthRatio`, `heightRatio`, `key`, `content`, `enabled`, `data`) or plain texts.": "",
  "A base cell in pixels; a tile is `widthRatio` × `heightRatio` of them.": "",
  "`horizontal`: the tiles fill the height in columns and the view scrolls sideways (give it a `height`); `vertical`: they fill the width in rows.": "",
  "`none`, `single` or `multiple`.": "",
  "The chosen tile (`single`): its `key`, else its index; the chosen tiles (`multiple`) as a list. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "The tiles can be put in another order by dragging, or with Ctrl and an arrow key.": "",
  "A CSS length or pixels.": "",
  "the kit’s “Tiles”": "",
  "A press on a tile that was not a drag (`index`, `item`, `event`); Enter on a focused tile too.": "",
  "The chosen tiles changed (`indexes`, `items`, `byUser`).": "",
  "A tile is about to be dragged or moved with the keys (`fromIndex`, `toIndex`); `cancel = true` keeps it.": "",
  "A tile was dropped or moved to a new place (`item`, `fromIndex`, `toIndex`): your data is yours to reorder.": "",
  "The chosen tiles’ indexes, in tile order.": "",
  "How many tiles there are.": "",
  "A tile is being dragged.": "",
  "Chooses a tile programmatically: the only one (`single`), or one more (`multiple`).": "",
  "Between a value (a key or an index) and a tile’s index.": ""
